'''Jecki Lon''' was a [[Theelin-human hybrid]] [[Gender|female]] [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] who lived during the [[High Republic Era]] in [[132 BBY]].<ref name="Timeline" /> She was the Padawan of [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]] and was calm and mature for her age.

==Biography==
===The Aniseya affair===
{{Quote|Why do you keep old holos of your former Padawan? This pastime encourages sentimentality and nostalgia. And both of these emotions can lead to&mdash;''"<br />"''Our memories are lessons. 'If we don't meditate on the past&hellip;'<nowiki/>''"<br />"''<nowiki/>'We're doomed to repeat it.'|Jecki Lon and Sol|<ref name="Lost / Found" />}}
[[Reproduction|Born]] around [[153 BBY]],<ref name="birth" /> Jecki Lon was at some point inducted into the [[Jedi Order]], where she served as a [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] apprenticed to [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]].<ref name="Lost / Found" />

In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Timeline" /> Lon intruded on Sol to relay Master [[Vernestra Rwoh]] for Sol to join her on the detention level. Having noticed her master observing a [[hologram]] of [[Verosha Aniseya|Verosha "Osha" Aniseya]], his former Padawan, Lon questioned the activity as a sign of attachment. Sol expressed the belief that memories could serve as lessons, preventing mistakes of the past from occurring again, an assessment Lon completed for him aloud. Lon then departed with Sol.<ref name="Lost / Found" />

Later, Lon joined Sol in an effort to apprehend Osha, who was wanted as a suspect for the [[Indara's murder|murder]] of Master [[Indara]], on [[Carlac]]. As it was Lon's first mission, Sol opined the need for backup in the form of [[Yord Fandar]], whom Lon believed often acted characteristically as himself. Sol and Lon found a surprised Fandar aboard their<ref name="Lost / Found" /> [[Polan-717 Jedi transport]]<ref name="Databank Polan">{{Databank|polan|Polan}}</ref> steaming his [[Jedi apparel|robes]] bare-chested, leading Lon to tell him to put his [[Clothing|clothes]] on.<ref name="Lost / Found" />

[[File:JeckiYord-LostFound.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Jecki Lon and Yord Fandar on Carlac]]
While traveling in [[hyperspace]], Lon asked Sol about his connection to Osha, causing him to share details about their past on [[Brendok]]. When Sol mentioned that Osha had a twin, [[Mae-ho Aniseya|Mae-ho “Mae” Aniseya]], Lon wondered whether she could be responsible for the murder, which her master denied on account of Mae's [[death]], an event he claimed to have witnessed firsthand.<ref name="Lost / Found" />

On Carlac, Fandar, Lon, and Sol explored the crashed<ref name="Lost / Found" /> [[DTE-CSA-17 Calaboose prison ship|DTE-CSA-17 Calaboose]] [[prison ship]] ''[[Palwick]]''<ref name="Databank Palwick">{{Databank|palwick-prison-ship|Palwick prison ship}}</ref> where Osha was held, tracking her through snowfall and into a cave. Sol prevented Osha from slipping off a ledge with [[the Force]], who informed Sol that Mae was alive. The Jedi Master believed Osha, who left the cave with the trio.<ref name="Lost / Found" />

===Investigation on Olega===
{{Quote|Uh, we secure the perimeter. Jecki stays on lookout, and I will confront this imposter. Stun him, if need be, then we bring him back to the ship for questioning.''"<br />"''Or we skip that, and she just talks to him. If he's Mae's accomplice, we can send her in, she can talk to him. We can record and monitor the conversation. That way, we have a lead on Mae, plus we also get a confession from him. It seems like the most logical way.|Yord Fandar and Jecki Lon|<ref name="Revenge / Justice" />}}
On board the Polnan, Lon struggled with entering command sequences into a control console. Osha, who had [[Sleep|slept]] in the [[Medical bay|medbay]], suggested that Lon repolarize the [[Starship|ship]]'s [[power coupling]]s. Lon did so successfully and asked if Osha was a [[pilot]], to which she clarified that she was a [[meknek]], something Lon considered dangerous work meant only for [[R2-series astromech droid|R2 series astromech droids]]. Osha replied that she was better company and more flexible than a droid.<ref name="Revenge / Justice" />

[[File:JeckiYordSolOshaonOlega-RevengeJustice.png|thumb|right|275px|Lon, Fandar, Sol, and Osha Aniseya]]
Master Rwoh transmitted a message to Sol, sending his team to investigate a break-in at the [[Olega Jedi temple|Jedi temple]] on [[Olega]] committed by an individual matching Osha's description. Lon accompanied Osha, Fandar, and Sol, who were greeted by a local Jedi. Another Jedi approached with a [[youngling]] who had activated the [[Jedi temple|temple]]'s [[Security droid|gatekeeper droid]]. Lon questioned the youngling, who indicated that they had been paid by someone who they believed was Osha.<ref name="Revenge / Justice" />

The group followed the two Jedi into the Olega temple to speak to Master [[Torbin]], only to find Osha, who had taken a shortcut, standing over Torbin's dead body. Osha offered an explanation, which Lon asked for, but Fandar defended her, having followed and watched her the whole time. Lon noticed that Torbin, who had ingested a poison, showed no signs of struggle, leading [[Sol]] to conclude that the Jedi Master had done so willingly.<ref name="Revenge / Justice" />

Osha told the others that the poison, bunta, did not last for long and must have come from nearby, leading Osha and the Jedi to surveil a nearby apothecary. Fandar suggested than Lon remained on lookout, but Jecki devised an alternate plan to use Osha and Mae's identical appearances to extract a confession from the shop keeper. Osha followed through, and the Jedi entered the apothecary, Lon informing the proprietor, [[The Stranger|Qimir]], that they had recorded his admission of guilt. Sol questioned Qimir, who explained that Mae wanted revenge on four Jedi, before sending Fandar to secure the perimeter and Lon to the ship, intending to return later to catch Mae.<ref name="Revenge / Justice" />

That night, Lon remained on comms aboard the Polnan while Fandar kept watch for Mae. Fandar identified Mae and Sol confronted her, leading to a fight between the two. Lon brought the ship above the conflict and, shining a spotlight on Osha, declared her under arrest and ordered her to stand down. Mae fled, leaving Lon without a visual and, after a brief encounter with Osha, escaped completely.<ref name="Revenge / Justice" />

===The Wookiee and the Sith===
{{Quote|You're under arrest for the murder of Master Indara, the murder of&mdash; The murder of Master Torbin, the murder of Master Kelnacca, and the fire that killed your family.|Jecki Lon attempting to arrest Mae-ho Aniseya whilst fighting her.|<ref name="Night" />}}
At the Jedi Temple, Lon trained with other students under the instruction of Jedi Master [[Lakshay]]. After the session, she was approached by Osha, who had come to say goodbye and thanked Lon for finding her sister and clearing her name, which the Padawan attributed to duty. Jecki implored Osha to stay, causing her to be teased by Osha about missing her, before observing that Osha cared about her twin, Mae. Osha promised to look Lon up the next time she was on Coruscant, offering to trade stories about Sol at a cantina. Lon asked whether Aniseya had spoken to Sol about her departure, which she did not want to, not wishing to trouble her former master.<ref name="Day" />

When Sol tried to look for Aniseya, Lon told her master that Osha had already left. He then decided to go look for her and eventually convinced her they needed her on their [[Mission to Khofar|mission]] to [[Khofar]] believing she would be able to convince [[Mae-ho Aniseya]] to peacefully come with them. On board the Polnan, Lon accompanied [[Sol]], [[Yord Fandar]], [[Verosha Aniseya]], [[Bazil]], [[Wellig Yuns]], [[Misha Sharuk]], [[Sen Bennex]] and [[Inro Jadrel]] to Khofar in search of the [[Wookiee]] [[Jedi]] [[Kelnacca]], Mae's next target. Verosha quietly conversed with Jecki about the group's tracker, Bazil, interrupting a mission briefing led by Fandar. Once on Khofar, Lon questioned an alien native using a translator, asking if he'd seen the Wookiee. While traversing the planet's [[forest]]s, Osha told Lon about an aggressive creature that she disturbed that Sol subsequently killed. The Padawan expressed that witnessing death and transformation into [[the Force]] was an honor, and Aniseya decided that she could not accept death as a true Jedi should, troubled by her past experiences with Mae. Lon assured her that people were defined by the experiences they had survived rather than their grief and loss.<ref name="Day" />

[[File:JeckiVsTheStranger-Night.png|thumb|left|250px|Jecki battles The Stranger on Khofar]]
The Jedi found Kelnacca dead and were confronted by a dark figure wielding a [[The Stranger's lightsaber|red lightsaber]]&mdash;Mae's [[The Stranger|master]]. When Jecki questioned what it was, he used the Force to push her and the others aside.<ref name="Day" /> Outside Kelnacca's abode, she ambushed an unsuspecting Mae,<ref name="Night" /> who had come to turn herself over to the Jedi,<ref name="Day" /> fighting her in hand-to-hand and attempting to place her in binders. Lon declared Aniseya under arrest, listing her crimes, but Mae continued to resist being placed into custody. Aniseya held a knife to Lon's throat, but the Padawn brought Mae to the ground and secured her binders.<ref name="Night" />

[[File:JeckisDead-Night.png|thumb|right|250px|Jecki is impaled by the Stranger's hidden shoto]]
Jecki called [[Kelnacca's lightsaber]] to her hand, but quickly sensed danger, reaching for [[Jecki Lon's lightsaber|her own weapon]]. Attacked by the lightsaber wielder, the figure commended Lon's loyalty to Mae, who had intended to betray him. The Padawan fought the mysterious adversary, but his armor disabled her lightsaber, causing her to draw Kelnaca's blade. Lon's saber quickly re-activated, and she dueled her opponent using Kelnacca's weapon [[Jar'Kai|in conjunction]] with her own until he destroyed the end of the Wookiee's blade. The Jedi continued to fight alongside Sol. Defending Mae when her master attacked her, Jecki disarmed the opposing duelist&mdash;revealed as Qimir&mdash;of his [[Cortosis|helmet]], before being stabbed three times in quick succession, killing her.<ref name="Night" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|Jecki.''"<br />"''Was that its name?''"<br />"''She was a child.''"<br />"''You brought her here.|Sol and the Stranger|<ref name="Night" />}}
Sol and Qimir spoke briefly about Lon immediately after her death. Sol berated Qimir for killing her, as she was only a child, but Qimir deflected the blame for her death back on Sol for bringing her into a combat zone.<ref name="Night" /> Her body was later found by Vernestra Rwoh and [[Mog Adana]] when they and another group of Jedi arrived at Khofar, after Sol sent a [[distress signal]]. Rwoh told Adana to retrieve the corpses of Lon and her comrades, so they could receive a proper burial.<ref name="Teach / Corrupt">{{Acolyte|Teach / Corrupt}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
[[File:JeckiBokkenSaber-Day.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Jecki Lon trained as a Padawan of the Jedi Order]]
{{Quote|Permission to speak freely, master?|Jecki Lon|<ref name="Lost / Found" />}}
Jecki Lon was calm and mature for her age.<ref name="DB" /> She consistently asked for permission from her Master to speak freely before doing so.<ref name="Lost / Found" />

==Powers and abilities==
Jecki knew how to [[Force push]], utilizing the ability against [[Mae-ho Aniseya|Mae Aniseya]] in their duel on [[Khofar]]. She was also quite skilled in [[Jar'Kai]], as she was able to dual-wield her lightsaber with the [[Kelnacca's lightsaber|lightsaber]] she retrieved from Mae, and hold her ground for some time against [[The Stranger|Qimir]].<ref name="Night" />

==Equipment==
[[File:JeckiSaber-DressingAcolyte.png|thumb|right|200px|Jecki Lon wielded a green-bladed lightsaber.]]
{{Quote|You took Master Kelnacca's saber.|Jecki Lon to Mae Aniseya, taking Kelnacca's lightsaber|<ref name="Night" />}}
As with many other [[Jedi]] during the [[High Republic Era]], Jecki wore [[Color|white]] and gold colored [[Temple robes|robes]] while at the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi temple]]. On her first mission with [[Sol|her Master]] she wore brown and gold [[Mission robes|field robes]]. She possessed a [[Jecki Lon's lightsaber|green-bladed lightsaber]].<ref name="Lost / Found" /> While training, Jecki wielded a [[Bokken saber]].<ref name="Day" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I think I saw a lot of me within [Jecki Lon]&mdash;in her kind of perfectionism, and how hard she is on herself. Also, she was such a different character from Lyra and Laura and Anna; it was really fun to play this much more constrained, put-together person. That was a challenge for me because I’m not used to that.|Dafne Keen|<ref name="Elle">{{WebCite|url=https://www.elle.com/culture/movies-tv/a60884751/dafne-keen-star-wars-the-acolyte-premiere-interview|text=Dafne Keen on The Acolyte, Introducing Jecki Lon, and Her Padmé-Inspired Premiere Look|author=Lauren Puckett-Pope|work=[https://www.elle.com/ Elle.com]|date=2024-05-24|archivedate=20240603102131}}</ref>}}
[[File:DafneCharlieBtS-Acolyte.jpg|230px|thumb|left|Dafne Keen and Charlie Barnett on set of ''The Acolyte''.]]
Jecki Lon was created for the [[2024]] [[Disney+]] live-action series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''<ref name="Interview" /> and is portrayed by [[Dafne Keen]].<ref name="Lost / Found credits">{{Acolyte|Lost / Found}} credits</ref> Lon was initially shown in the first official trailer for the series on [[March 19]], [[2024]]<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|BtytYWhg2mc|The Acolyte &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+}}</ref> before simultaneously appearing in "[[Lost / Found]]" and "[[Revenge / Justice]]," the first two episodes of the series,<ref name="Lost / Found" /> which were released on [[June 4]] of the same year.<ref name="Announcement">{{SW|url=news/the-acolyte-teaser-poster|text=''The Acolyte'' Teaser Poster, Premiere Date Revealed}}</ref>

It was a dream of series creator [[Leslye Headland]] to create a Theelin Jedi character, having loved the character of [[Rystáll Sant]] from the [[1997]] [[The Star Wars Trilogy Special Edition|Special Edition]] re-release of the [[1983]] film {{Film|VI}}, the last installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[original trilogy]].<ref name="Interview" /> She also said a significant motivation was wanting to cast Keen, as she wanted "to see X-23 with a lightsaber."<ref name="IGN">{{WebCite|url=https://www.ign.com/articles/star-wars-the-acolyte-showrunner-on-how-itll-challenge-what-we-know-about-the-jedi-and-sith|text=''The Acolyte'' Showrunner on How It'll Challenge What We Know About the Jedi and Sith|archivedate=20240612055532}}</ref> Concept art for Jecki Lon depicts her as [[human]].<ref name="Costumes">{{SWYouTube|eZ8uYxZv8Lg|The Acolyte &#124; Jennifer Bryan - Jedi Costumes &#124; Disney+}}</ref> 

[[File:DafneKeen-Hoodie.jpg|230px|thumb|right|Dafne Keen behind the scenes]]
Keen stated that, in her mind, Jecki Lon developed a crush on Osha, and the actor played the character as such in the episode "[[Day (episode)|Day]]." She describes her portrayal of the Jedi as an eighteen-year-old with limited interactions with others, developing such feelings&mdash;including the accompanying "guilt and confusion" given the Jedi Order's ban on attachments&mdash;for the first time. Keen also enjoyed playing Jecki Lon for the sense of competition and later friendship between her character and Osha.<ref name="Queer Lon">{{WebCite|url=https://decider.com/2024/06/19/the-acolyte-dafne-keen-confirms-jecki-lon-queer-romance-with-amandla-stenberg-osha|text=‘The Acolyte’ Just Got Even More Queer: Dafne Keen Confirms Jecki Lon is Crushing on Amandla Stenberg's Osha|author=Meghan O'Keefe|date=2024-06-19|work=''Decider''|archivedate=20240619192212}}</ref>

